  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 2: THE ANCHOR STIRS"
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "That night, camped in the lee of a wind-scoured butte, the stillness in Geralt’s mind… changed."
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "For eight years, it had been a quiet pool—the Companion Protocol’s presence was like a distant, comforting star."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "Now, the pool had currents."
  - line: 80
    type: narration
    text: "He dreamt not in images, but in architectures."
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "He saw the triune schematic of Luminaire—Sound, Light, Anchor—as a rotating, crystalline model."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "Then he saw it fracture, the Light bleeding away into Needles, the Sound shattering into fragments, the Anchor… hook into a specific resonance frequency."
  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "His frequency."
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "He woke with a gasp, the desert cold around him."
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck was already awake, watching him."
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "“You glowed,” Oreck stated. “Like a banked coal."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "Your scars."
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "The ones from the Hub.”"
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt looked at his hands."
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "The old neural interface scars, pale against his skin, were fading even as he watched."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "Not healing."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Integrating."
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "< Biological assimilation ongoing."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Anchor symbiosis at 41%."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "Stability maintained. > the applicator reported."
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "Why now? he thought."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "The armor answered, not with words, but with a felt concept—a pressure against his sternum, like a hand pushing him east."
  - line: 103
    type: narration
    text: "Danger."
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "Convergence."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "“The Federation scare it awake?” Oreck asked, somehow intuiting the unspoken conversation."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "“Maybe."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "Or it’s something else.”"
  - line: 111
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

